  "chapter": 398,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                 APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 8 Chapter 398\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2805, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the economic development law, in relation to estab-\n        lishing   entrepreneurship  assistance  centers;  to  amend  the\n        economic development law and  the  labor  law,  in  relation  to\n        making  technical  corrections  relating  thereto; and to repeal\n        article 9 of the economic development law relating thereto\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill seeks to amend provisions of  the  New  York  State  Omnibus\nEconomic  Development  Act (the \"Act\") which created the Entrepreneurial\nAssistance Program (EAP) in 1987. Since its creation, the EAP has helped\nentrepreneurs create new businesses and has provided in-depth assistance\nto minorities, women, dislocated workers and individuals with a disabil-\nity interested in starting a business. The Act allows for the  provision\nof  funding to development centers and entrepreneurship support centers,\nboth of which have been instrumental in  increasing  business  ownership\namong  these  groups,  supporting  minority and women-owned start-ups to\ntransition to small-growth companies, increasing  access  to  financing,\nand  expanding  sales  by  minority,  women,  disabled and veteran owned\nfirms, creating private-sector jobs, and more.\n \n  The bill seeks to streamline the Act by combining the requirements for\ndevelopment centers and  entrepreneurship  support  centers  into  newly\ncreated  Entrepreneurship Assistance Centers (EAC) while maintaining the\npurpose of the program. While I support improving program  efficiencies,\nas  drafted, this bill would have the unintended effect of adding unnec-\nessary requirements on EAP and would provide an  additional  administra-\ntive  burden  on already overextended centers. The Executive has secured\nan agreement with the Legislature to pass legislation  in  the  upcoming\nsession  to  minimize  these  additional  requirements and address these\nconcerns. On this basis, I am signing this bill.\n \nThis bill is approved.                        (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2018
 },
